  1368                              <1> ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return AL = 0 if it
  1369                              <1> ; was ')' and 2 if it was ']'. Brackets of both kinds count together;
  1370                              <1> ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for '\' with
  1371                              <1> ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
  1372                              <1> ; anyway). ECX counts the open levels, from 1 for the one we are in.
  1373                              <1> ;
